016 - All People That on Earth Do Dwell
William Kethe / Louis Bourgeois
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: 96
Number: 16
Topic: Worship - Adoration and Praise

Verse 1:
[G]All people [Em]that [Bm]on [Em]earth [D]do [G]dwell,
[G]Sing to the [D]Lord [Em]with [C]cheerful [D]voice;
[Em]Him [D/F#]serve [G]with mirth, [C]His [D7/A]praise [G]forth tell,
[D]Come ye [Am]before [Bm]Him [D]and rejoice.

Verse 2:
[G]Know that [D]the [Em]Lord [Bm]is [Em]God [D]indeed;
[G]Without our [D]aid [Em]He [C]did [G]us [D]make;
[Em]We [D/F#]are [G]His folk, [C]He [D7/A]doth [G]us feed,
[D]And for [Am]His sheep [Bm]He [D]doth us [G]take.

Verse 3:
[G]O enter [D]then [Em]His [Bm]gates [D]with [G]praise,
[G]Approach with [D]joy [Em]His [C]courts [G]unto;
[Em]Praise, [D/F#]laud, [G]and bless [C]His [D7/A]name [G]always,
[D]For it [Am]is seemly [D]so to [G]do.

Verse 4:
[G]For why [D]the [Em]Lord [Bm]our [Em]God [D]is [G]good,
[G]His mercy [D]is [Em]forever [D]sure;
[Em]His [D/F#]truth [G]at [D]all [G/B]times firmly stood,
[D]And shall [Am]from age [Bm]to [D]age endure.
